# librsvg -- renders SVG, and ships the gdk-pixbuf SVG loader.
#
# This is the icon half of the same gap libjxl closes for wallpapers. gdk-pixbuf
# 2.42.12 has no SVG loader of its own -- the loader lives HERE -- and
# adwaita-icon-theme, already in this tree, is 644 symbolic icons plus 75
# scalable ones, all SVG. Without this package every one of them fails to
# decode: the theme installs, the build is green, and the desktop draws missing
# image placeholders where its icons should be.
#
# THE SECOND PACKAGE IN THIS TREE WRITTEN IN RUST, and the first that also has C
# dependencies. It builds in duct/rust rather than duct/chroot, like
# uutils-coreutils, because the Duct package set contains no Rust compiler --
# see RUST_PKGS in the Makefile.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env. BLFS
# 12.4 carries 2.61.0.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/librsvg/2.61/librsvg-2.61.0.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=dbd0db40a1179a382fbb8cc930837671b973d722ba106a3dee2aad0fd858e2c4
SRC_DIR=librsvg-2.61.0

# THIS PACKAGE REACHES THE NETWORK DURING ITS BUILD, and that is deliberate
# rather than overlooked.
#
# The tarball ships Cargo.lock and NO vendor/ directory -- verified, not assumed
# -- so cargo fetches every crate from crates.io. It is the same exception
# uutils-coreutils already documents as "the one network access in the whole
# pipeline", and it is why both live in RUST_PKGS and build in an image that has
# a CA bundle, rather than in duct/chroot which deliberately has neither curl
# nor wget.
#
# --locked IS ALREADY HANDLED BY UPSTREAM AND MUST NOT BE REMOVED FROM THE
# EQUATION BY SWITCHING BUILD PATHS. meson/cargo_wrapper.py passes it on all
# three of its cargo paths -- line 148 (cbuild), 153 (test), 161 (build) -- so
# this recipe does not need to add it. It matters for the reason uutils' own
# build.sh spells out: without --locked, cargo is free to REWRITE Cargo.lock
# when it considers it stale, silently resolving crate versions other than the
# ones the tarball shipped and verified. Recorded here because the flag is
# invisible from this file, and a future change that drives cargo directly
# instead of through the wrapper would drop it without anything noticing.
#
# cargo-c is a HARD requirement, not a convenience: meson.build:27 is
#   cargo_c = find_program('cargo-cbuild', version:'>= 0.10.0')
# with NO required:false, so a missing cargo-cbuild is a configure failure.
#
# It is a DUCT PACKAGE and is declared in [dependencies.build]. This comment
# previously said it came "from the build image, not from a Duct package", which
# was true when this recipe was written and stopped being true when cargo-c was
# packaged. Declaring it is not documentation: tools/dep-levels.sh reads
# [dependencies.build] to assign CI build levels, so an undeclared cargo-c could
# be scheduled at the same level as librsvg or after it.

# -Dpixbuf-loader=enabled IS LOAD-BEARING. Its default is **auto**, and the
# loader is the entire reason this package is in the tree. An auto feature that
# cannot find gdk-pixbuf-query-loaders switches itself off and the build still
# succeeds -- the identical failure shape as libjxl's gdk-pixbuf plugin, which
# warns and returns rather than erroring. Pinned to `enabled` so a missing
# prerequisite is a hard configure error instead of a silently missing loader,
# and asserted on disk in install.sh regardless, because the flag being right
# and the artefact existing are two different facts.
#
# -Dpixbuf=enabled for the same reason one level up: it is also `auto`, and it
# gates the loader.
#
# -Dintrospection=enabled: also `auto`. gjs-based code and gnome-shell reach
# librsvg through the typelib, and an auto feature that quietly found no
# g-ir-scanner would produce a library usable from C and invisible to
# JavaScript.
#
# -Ddocs=disabled: needs gi-docgen AND rst2man (python-docutils); neither is
# packaged. -Dvala=disabled: vala is not packaged. Both are `auto` and would
# switch themselves off here anyway -- pinned because a soft-skip that happens
# to do what is wanted today is not a decision, and because BLFS builds this
# package WITH vala, so the divergence should be visible rather than inferred.
#
# -Davif=disabled: embedded AVIF needs libdav1d (meson.build:76), which is not
# packaged. `auto` again. Consequence worth knowing: an SVG with an embedded
# AVIF image renders without that image. No GNOME 48 icon or wallpaper uses one.
#
# -Dtests=false: the suite needs reference renderings and Xorg fonts, and BLFS
# notes one test is known to fail even with them.
MESON_ARGS="-Dpixbuf=enabled -Dpixbuf-loader=enabled -Dintrospection=enabled \
-Ddocs=disabled -Dvala=disabled -Davif=disabled -Dtests=false"
